// The sheet's own delivery is a conjured floating weapon that makes its own
// melee spell attack, re-thrown at any target it can reach each round as a
// bonus action; there is no summoned-pet/conjured-weapon-entity mechanism
// in this engine to model the "floating weapon" itself, so this ships as a
// direct player-triggered melee strike -- same simplification precedent as
// every other conjured-weapon spell in this batch (flame_blade.ron). The
// 18 m range is dropped (it only governed where the weapon could be
// summoned/moved, not the strike's own reach, per the sheet's own notes);
// the strike itself is melee range, matching the sheet's explicit "the
// strike itself is melee reach."
//
// Sear is used over Stab/Slash/Bash/Hook for the closest available flavor
// match to "raw force" -- its hardcoded kind is Energy, not Force (no
// MeleeConstructorKind exposes a real Force damage_kind field, see
// booming_blade.ron, Wave 1, for the full reasoning), but Energy reads
// closer to an unworldly force strike than Piercing/Slashing/Crushing
// would.
//
// The sheet's own duration is Secs(60) ("re-attack each round ... for the
// duration"), but there is no persistent-conjured-weapon-summon mechanism
// that would need a real 60 s timer (same situation as flame_blade.ron in
// this batch) -- the compendium entry below lists duration: Instant rather
// than Secs(60) for the same reason divine_favor.ron (Wave 1) does. `Bonus`
// cast_time is kept as flavor metadata only (matches how every gravesong
// smite and healing_word.ron, Wave 1, already treat non-Action cast times --
// there is no real turn economy to enforce it against).
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 35,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Sear(damage: 26, poise: 5, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
